WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.750
- I have no idea you were together.

00:00:02.604 --> 00:00:04.620
I don't know private lives.

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:06.270
I never know people's private lives.

00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:07.357
And I literally was like,

00:00:07.357 --> 00:00:08.640
"You and Rita were together".

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:10.650
I had no idea, I only know people's work.

00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:12.217
- I have that same reaction most days.

00:00:12.217 --> 00:00:14.310
- Like, I know, I love her.

00:00:14.310 --> 00:00:16.159
She's so talented and so sweet.

00:00:16.159 --> 00:00:17.460
- Yeah, she is.
- Yeah, got a good one.

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:19.560
Anyway, well, welcome to our show.

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:20.850
I just moved here to New York City.

00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:21.690
Do you like coming here?

00:00:21.690 --> 00:00:23.100
- I love coming here.

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:24.334
Yeah.

00:00:24.334 --> 00:00:25.950
It's the big smoke.

00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:27.060
It's the fast lane.

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:27.933
A lot of people.

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:30.150
My favorite thing is food.

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:31.950
I love just to come here and eat.

00:00:31.950 --> 00:00:34.363
- [Kelly] I know.
- Great restaurants.

00:00:34.363 --> 00:00:36.510
And I just go wandering the
streets and just look at people.

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:37.860
- Especially Christmas time, yeah.

00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:39.630
I just love like, any
kind of holiday time.

00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:40.890
'Cause it'll lit up,

00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:42.120
is like, it feels like you're in a movie.

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:43.770
Well you are in a movie a lot of times,

00:00:43.770 --> 00:00:46.505
so you probably feel that a lot, yeah.

00:00:46.505 --> 00:00:48.780
Well you have two daughters, right?

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:49.950
- Two daughters, yeah.

00:00:49.950 --> 00:00:50.783
Yeah.

00:00:50.783 --> 00:00:53.550
TK and Matewa, they're 11 and 9.

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:55.680
- [Kelly] I have a nine
year old as as well.

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:56.513
- [Taika] That's me.

00:00:56.513 --> 00:00:57.900
- So this is behind the scenes.

00:00:57.900 --> 00:00:59.220
- Imparting my knowledge.

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:01.590
And they're doing great
to pretend that they care.

00:01:01.590 --> 00:01:03.150
- I was gonna say, are
they interested though?

00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:04.620
Because you take them on set, right?

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:05.453
- They are interested.

00:01:05.453 --> 00:01:07.440
They, you know, I think they...

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:10.890
I mean, they've been on all
of the sets of everything.

00:01:10.890 --> 00:01:13.410
They've been in, you know,
like a couple of little extra.

00:01:13.410 --> 00:01:14.603
- I know in Thor, yeah.

00:01:14.603 --> 00:01:17.963
- In Thor I put my youngest
daughter in, Matewa.

00:01:17.963 --> 00:01:20.875
That was from the set of Thor.

00:01:20.875 --> 00:01:21.708
And it was funny.

00:01:21.708 --> 00:01:22.950
She said, "I wanna be in the film".

00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:25.770
And then she didn't realize
she had to work all day.

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:26.792
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:26.792 --> 00:01:28.740
- And we did like, I think
I did one or two takes,

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:31.440
and she was in a scene
with Christian Bale.

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:33.570
You know, one of the greats of all time.

00:01:33.570 --> 00:01:35.910
And after two takes, she
walked off and came up to me

00:01:35.910 --> 00:01:37.850
and she said, "Okay, gimme my money".

00:01:37.850 --> 00:01:38.947
(audience laughs)

00:01:38.947 --> 00:01:39.780
- Oh My God.

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:40.613
- And I said,

00:01:40.613 --> 00:01:42.090
"No darling, you have to
keep doing this all day".

00:01:42.090 --> 00:01:43.140
She said, "All day?".

00:01:43.140 --> 00:01:44.437
- Know your worth, though.

00:01:44.437 --> 00:01:46.477
(both laugh)

00:01:46.477 --> 00:01:48.840
- "I've got two good
takes of me, now pay me".

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:49.980
- Oh my God.

00:01:49.980 --> 00:01:50.813
It is funny,

00:01:50.813 --> 00:01:51.810
your kids though, they see
what you do and they think--

00:01:51.810 --> 00:01:54.060
'Cause my kids have gone
with me to like award shows

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:55.087
and they're like,

00:01:55.087 --> 00:01:56.070
"So, when are we leaving?"

00:01:56.070 --> 00:01:58.207
And I'm like, "Are you outta your mind?"

00:01:58.207 --> 00:02:00.211
- "Like, look at these people".

00:02:00.211 --> 00:02:01.370
- "We've been here 10 minutes".

00:02:01.370 --> 00:02:03.660
And they're like, "When
can we get ice cream?"

00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:05.130
I'm like, "Okay, cool".

00:02:05.130 --> 00:02:05.963
You just had,

00:02:05.963 --> 00:02:07.920
you celebrated your first
anniversary, right, with Rita?

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:09.630
- Yes, Rita and I have been
married for over a year.

00:02:09.630 --> 00:02:10.463
- That's amazing.

00:02:10.463 --> 00:02:12.810
I heard there was an Elvis
impersonator at your wedding.

00:02:12.810 --> 00:02:13.800
Was that planned?

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:15.930
- [Taika] Randomly an Elvis
impersonator was there.

00:02:15.930 --> 00:02:16.854
I didn't organize that.

00:02:16.854 --> 00:02:17.910
Neither did Rita.

00:02:17.910 --> 00:02:19.170
- How is there randomly...

00:02:19.170 --> 00:02:21.333
Look at how incredibly hot she is.

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:24.556
How do they randomly end up at your...

00:02:24.556 --> 00:02:25.893
That's amazing.

00:02:26.820 --> 00:02:27.690
- I've got a couple of friends

00:02:27.690 --> 00:02:29.070
who like to do things like that.

00:02:29.070 --> 00:02:29.933
- [Kelly] That's fun.

00:02:30.867 --> 00:02:33.210
- And you know, Rami
Malek actually organized

00:02:33.210 --> 00:02:37.170
for a Freddie Mercury
impersonator at my birthday

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:39.840
a year or two before that.

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:40.673
- [Kelly] I love your friends.

00:02:40.673 --> 00:02:41.702
- I was like,

00:02:41.702 --> 00:02:42.798
"Why wouldn't you just do it yourself?"

00:02:42.798 --> 00:02:43.631
(audience laughs)

00:02:43.631 --> 00:02:44.520
- That would've been way funnier.

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:45.780
Yeah.

00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:46.613
Like, "No, we just
wanted to embarrass you".

00:02:46.613 --> 00:02:48.360
I heard that she actually
proposed to you as well.

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:49.290
- She proposed to me.

00:02:49.290 --> 00:02:51.543
I mean, we do things really topsy-turvy.

00:02:52.965 --> 00:02:55.962
She proposed to me, you know,

00:02:55.962 --> 00:02:57.180
she's great.

00:02:57.180 --> 00:02:58.200
You just don't say no to Rita.

00:02:58.200 --> 00:02:59.802
That's one of the things.

00:02:59.802 --> 00:03:00.779
(laughs)

00:03:00.779 --> 00:03:02.340
- She's very powerful.
- She's very powerful.

00:03:02.340 --> 00:03:03.173
She proposed to me.

00:03:03.173 --> 00:03:04.650
Before that when we first got together,

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:06.690
after a couple of weeks, we had dinner.

00:03:06.690 --> 00:03:07.807
And she said,

00:03:07.807 --> 00:03:10.410
"You know, when people
say they get together

00:03:10.410 --> 00:03:11.820
and they say, let's just take it slow

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:12.883
and see what happens and all that".

00:03:12.883 --> 00:03:15.270
I was like, "Yeah, yeah. I know that one".

00:03:15.270 --> 00:03:17.464
And she said, "Well,
we're not doing that".

00:03:17.464 --> 00:03:19.112
- Just right off the bat?

00:03:19.112 --> 00:03:20.220
- [Taika] We're going all in.

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:21.053
- That's pretty sexy.

00:03:21.053 --> 00:03:22.650
- It's very, very, very sexy.

00:03:22.650 --> 00:03:23.940
- If it works, you know?

00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:25.010
- Yeah, if it works.

00:03:25.010 --> 00:03:26.362
- If it's working,

00:03:26.362 --> 00:03:28.477
then you're like, "Wait, this is crazy".

00:03:28.477 --> 00:03:30.502
- An abduction situation.

00:03:30.502 --> 00:03:31.335
- Yeah, it worked out.

00:03:31.335 --> 00:03:33.961
Did she sign you up to do a Shrek Airbnb?

00:03:33.961 --> 00:03:34.794
- [Taika] Yeah.

00:03:34.794 --> 00:03:37.050
- Because I saw this
footage and it's incredible.

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:39.030
- Most of the great and
interesting things in my life

00:03:39.030 --> 00:03:40.650
is because of Rita, I'd say that.

00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:42.120
- She's very random, I love it.

00:03:42.120 --> 00:03:43.560
- She is, yeah.

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:47.040
An article came out that Airbnb
had made this Shrek replica

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:48.600
of Shrek's House.
- [Kelly] Sure.

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:49.590
- In the middle of Scotland,

00:03:49.590 --> 00:03:52.320
like way out in the middle of nowhere.

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:53.310
And, yeah.

00:03:53.310 --> 00:03:55.708
- You look so creepy in this picture.

00:03:55.708 --> 00:03:57.420
- And listen, everyone would
think that we had a photo,

00:03:57.420 --> 00:03:58.530
you know, camera crew and stuff.

00:03:58.530 --> 00:04:01.350
That was just us two driving
to the middle of nowhere.

00:04:01.350 --> 00:04:02.700
She painted herself green.

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:05.130
She revealed she had
brought these costumes

00:04:05.130 --> 00:04:06.993
and that we were getting content.

00:04:07.890 --> 00:04:09.390
- Oh my gosh.

00:04:09.390 --> 00:04:10.958
And you were like, "All right".

00:04:10.958 --> 00:04:13.481
- I didn't realize this
romantic trip was about content.

00:04:13.481 --> 00:04:16.320
- I just love picturing being romantic

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:18.479
looking like those characters.

00:04:18.479 --> 00:04:20.179
- [Taika] Being romantic?
- Yeah.

00:04:21.270 --> 00:04:24.540
That would be really
hard for me to ignore.

00:04:24.540 --> 00:04:25.373
- Yeah.

00:04:25.373 --> 00:04:26.206
And our accents...

00:04:27.270 --> 00:04:28.560
- Oh no, we have your accents.

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:29.760
Let's hear your Shrek accents.

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:30.593
Here we go.

00:04:30.593 --> 00:04:31.426
We've got some footage.

00:04:33.390 --> 00:04:34.740
- Who's this?

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:36.740
Fiona, I told you I don't like visitors.

00:04:39.051 --> 00:04:40.470
- Oh, don't mind him.

00:04:40.470 --> 00:04:43.173
Oh, old grump plaid pants.

00:04:43.173 --> 00:04:44.700
He's just an ogre.

00:04:44.700 --> 00:04:46.596
He means no harm.

00:04:46.596 --> 00:04:49.805
- [Taika] Turn around,
don't hear that woman.

00:04:49.805 --> 00:04:52.671
(applause)

00:04:52.671 --> 00:04:53.937
- Yeah.

00:04:53.937 --> 00:04:55.604
- [Kelly] Oh my God.

00:04:56.457 --> 00:04:57.990
- I'd say my accent is better.

00:04:57.990 --> 00:04:59.740
My accent's better than hers, sure.

00:05:00.930 --> 00:05:03.540
- I'm going say I can't get
away from the fact that y'all,

00:05:03.540 --> 00:05:06.960
like, I really hope you
made out in those costumes.

00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:09.000
- There was no, there's no way I could

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:11.850
with a big rubber mask on.

00:05:11.850 --> 00:05:15.030
- We did that and we sat there
in these ridiculous outfits

00:05:15.030 --> 00:05:18.450
eating dinner in Shrek's house.

00:05:18.450 --> 00:05:21.607
And then after she washed
the paint off her face.

00:05:21.607 --> 00:05:23.130
"Okay, well we did that, now what?"

00:05:23.130 --> 00:05:24.990
- Oh my God.
- And then we left.

00:05:24.990 --> 00:05:26.580
- But how funny is that?

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:29.130
I just love the randomness,
what a fun relationship.

00:05:29.130 --> 00:05:30.600
- [Taika] Yeah.
- Couple goals, I like it.

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:34.410
- Now let's look at his new
movie, which he directed.

00:05:34.410 --> 00:05:36.510
It's called Next Goal Wins.

00:05:36.510 --> 00:05:38.160
So this is actually an adaptation

00:05:38.160 --> 00:05:39.600
from a British documentary, right?

00:05:39.600 --> 00:05:40.440
- It's a true story.

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:43.140
Yeah, they made a documentary
about this in 2014.

00:05:43.140 --> 00:05:43.980
And it's the true story

00:05:43.980 --> 00:05:46.413
of the worst soccer team in the world.

00:05:47.384 --> 00:05:49.830
And this team from American Samoa,

00:05:49.830 --> 00:05:52.410
in 2001, they suffered
the biggest defeat ever.

00:05:52.410 --> 00:05:55.050
And just to, for some context,

00:05:55.050 --> 00:05:58.170
the team and the country have never,

00:05:58.170 --> 00:06:01.920
up until this point, had never
won a game or scored a goal,

00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:02.753
ever.

00:06:02.753 --> 00:06:03.598
- Or scored a goal?

00:06:03.598 --> 00:06:04.500
- Or scored a single goal.

00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:06.600
And they lost to Australia.

00:06:06.600 --> 00:06:08.040
And this is still the biggest record

00:06:08.040 --> 00:06:10.710
for biggest loss in an international game.

00:06:10.710 --> 00:06:12.828
They lost to Australia, 31-0.

00:06:12.828 --> 00:06:14.027
(audience moans)

00:06:14.027 --> 00:06:15.690
- I know, that would put most people off

00:06:15.690 --> 00:06:16.980
and deter you from, you know,

00:06:16.980 --> 00:06:18.630
ever wanting to get on the pitch again.

00:06:18.630 --> 00:06:21.900
But they pushed through,
they worked through it,

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:26.460
and they just got up and
literally tightened their laces

00:06:26.460 --> 00:06:28.140
and they got a new coach,

00:06:28.140 --> 00:06:30.180
played by Michael Fassbender in the movie.

00:06:30.180 --> 00:06:32.190
And this is the sort of really lovely,

00:06:32.190 --> 00:06:33.509
joyous, uplifting story,

00:06:33.509 --> 00:06:37.324
true story of these underdogs
who just wouldn't quit.

00:06:37.324 --> 00:06:38.770
- Yeah, I love an underdog story.

00:06:38.770 --> 00:06:39.810
Is that what kind of drew you to do it?

00:06:39.810 --> 00:06:40.643
- Yeah, yeah.

00:06:40.643 --> 00:06:41.850
I mean I love underdogs.

00:06:41.850 --> 00:06:44.956
I love, you know, just
exploring people on the margins.

00:06:44.956 --> 00:06:48.210
You know, and I mean I
was always at school,

00:06:48.210 --> 00:06:50.280
obviously very popular.

00:06:50.280 --> 00:06:52.191
(audience laughs)

00:06:52.191 --> 00:06:53.641
- We would've been friends.

00:06:53.641 --> 00:06:56.063
- But you know, I was like
taking people under my wing.

00:06:56.063 --> 00:06:59.340
And maybe, it was me being
taken under their wing.

00:06:59.340 --> 00:07:01.110
I think like bringing people together

00:07:01.110 --> 00:07:03.060
in some sort of team situation.

00:07:03.060 --> 00:07:05.200
Is just like forming a family, you know?

00:07:05.200 --> 00:07:06.033
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:07:06.033 --> 00:07:06.866
- You kind of support each other.

00:07:06.866 --> 00:07:07.929
- That's what I loved about sports.

00:07:07.929 --> 00:07:08.762
- You look after each other.

00:07:08.762 --> 00:07:09.780
Sports is great for
bringing people together.

00:07:09.780 --> 00:07:10.613
- Yeah, sports and theater.

00:07:10.613 --> 00:07:11.850
All that kind of stuff I loved as a kid,

00:07:11.850 --> 00:07:13.470
'cause that's where you find your people.

00:07:13.470 --> 00:07:14.397
- [Taika] Yeah.
- Yeah, your friends.

00:07:14.397 --> 00:07:17.040
- And it's set in the Pacific
Islands, where I'm from.

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:19.500
And it was a great opportunity
for me to come home

00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:22.050
and show indigenous people on screen,

00:07:22.050 --> 00:07:23.760
which is sort of my thing.

00:07:23.760 --> 00:07:25.170
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- I do that a lot.

00:07:25.170 --> 00:07:26.770
- And you wanna see a shift
in that representation?

00:07:26.770 --> 00:07:27.750
- Yeah, I do.

00:07:27.750 --> 00:07:29.610
Because like, you know, we
just had a really great show

00:07:29.610 --> 00:07:32.460
that my friend Sterlin
Harjo and I created,

00:07:32.460 --> 00:07:33.480
called Reservation Dogs.

00:07:33.480 --> 00:07:34.313
Which did really well.

00:07:34.313 --> 00:07:35.680
It's a fantastic TV show

00:07:36.540 --> 00:07:39.360
set on a reservation in Oklahoma.

00:07:39.360 --> 00:07:43.260
And you know, what I want is
for that to be a common thing

00:07:43.260 --> 00:07:45.690
and a regular thing as
opposed to, you know.

00:07:45.690 --> 00:07:46.523
'Cause everyone's like,

00:07:46.523 --> 00:07:47.940
"Wow, this is the first thing
we've seen in, you know,

00:07:47.940 --> 00:07:50.280
the last 10 years with
native representation".

00:07:50.280 --> 00:07:52.140
I was like, "That's not good".

00:07:52.140 --> 00:07:52.973
- Yeah.

00:07:52.973 --> 00:07:54.150
Don't give me that compliment.

00:07:54.150 --> 00:07:55.080
- Yeah, that's right.

00:07:55.080 --> 00:07:56.070
- Yeah, you don't want the compliment.

00:07:56.070 --> 00:07:57.270
You want it to be more normalized.

00:07:57.270 --> 00:07:58.410
- Yeah.

00:07:58.410 --> 00:08:00.660
And just like, tackling diversity

00:08:00.660 --> 00:08:02.308
without it being tokenism.

00:08:02.308 --> 00:08:03.141
- [Kelly] Absolutely.

00:08:03.141 --> 00:08:04.260
- And putting the stories

00:08:04.260 --> 00:08:07.350
into the hands of the
people who are from there.

00:08:07.350 --> 00:08:09.180
- Yeah, absolutely, 'cause
who better to tell it.

00:08:09.180 --> 00:08:10.013
- Exactly.

00:08:10.013 --> 00:08:12.600
- I also love this about you,
'cause obviously I love music.

00:08:12.600 --> 00:08:14.280
You're quite the DJ on set, I hear.

00:08:14.280 --> 00:08:15.600
Like, you have playlists.

00:08:15.600 --> 00:08:16.433
- I do have playlists.

00:08:16.433 --> 00:08:17.460
I play a lot of music.

00:08:17.460 --> 00:08:19.650
On Fridays I let the crew decide.

00:08:19.650 --> 00:08:21.430
- I was gonna say, do
you let anybody else?

00:08:21.430 --> 00:08:22.920
- A have a little
whiteboard, and they come.

00:08:22.920 --> 00:08:23.910
But it's so random

00:08:23.910 --> 00:08:25.350
between the different people on a crew.

00:08:25.350 --> 00:08:27.810
Like it is really one of
the worst radio sessions.

00:08:27.810 --> 00:08:28.950
- Oh my God.

00:08:28.950 --> 00:08:30.480
You would hate my Sirius channel.

00:08:30.480 --> 00:08:31.313
'Cause that's what it is.

00:08:31.313 --> 00:08:32.160
It's so random.

00:08:32.160 --> 00:08:34.210
It will go from Frank Sinatra to Nirvana.

00:08:35.190 --> 00:08:36.133
It will, yes.

00:08:36.133 --> 00:08:37.357
Yeah, I love that though.

00:08:37.357 --> 00:08:38.190
- Yeah.

00:08:38.190 --> 00:08:39.023
- Because then it's how
you like learn new music.

00:08:39.023 --> 00:08:40.187
- This is great to include
the team and like, you know,

00:08:40.187 --> 00:08:42.220
I mean the crew who are the team.

00:08:42.220 --> 00:08:43.230
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:08:43.230 --> 00:08:46.320
- And music I think, you know,
as we all know it just...

00:08:46.320 --> 00:08:47.970
Silence is just so awkward.

00:08:47.970 --> 00:08:49.260
And on set when you're sitting

00:08:49.260 --> 00:08:51.060
and everyone's being very silent,

00:08:51.060 --> 00:08:52.440
you feel like something's wrong.

00:08:52.440 --> 00:08:56.040
And I like just having music
and just fun and dance.

00:08:56.040 --> 00:09:00.331
And just to create a very
mellow and relax time.

00:09:00.331 --> 00:09:01.590
- Does the playlist affect
like what's going on?

00:09:01.590 --> 00:09:02.790
Do you ever make playlists specifically

00:09:02.790 --> 00:09:05.100
for this day we're shooting this?

00:09:05.100 --> 00:09:06.600
- Well I think when, you know,

00:09:06.600 --> 00:09:09.390
when there are various takes
where the sound doesn't matter.

00:09:09.390 --> 00:09:10.470
When the actors are doing stuff,

00:09:10.470 --> 00:09:12.840
I'll play certain things like, you know,

00:09:12.840 --> 00:09:15.090
for characters coming in

00:09:15.090 --> 00:09:16.260
and it's quite an intense situation,

00:09:16.260 --> 00:09:18.626
I might play the
soundtrack to The Shining.

00:09:18.626 --> 00:09:20.176
(audience laughs)
- Oh my God.

00:09:21.016 --> 00:09:22.080
- Or it's like a really tragic,

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:24.300
over the top, really melodramatic moment,

00:09:24.300 --> 00:09:27.510
it might be the Adagio piece from Platoon.

00:09:27.510 --> 00:09:30.357
- Oh My God, from Platoon?

00:09:30.357 --> 00:09:31.710
That's amazing.

00:09:31.710 --> 00:09:33.570
- Yeah, ordinary, ridiculous,
Sesame Street music.

00:09:33.570 --> 00:09:34.403
Whatever it is.
- I love it.

00:09:34.403 --> 00:09:35.520
- Just to kind of elevate the mood

00:09:35.520 --> 00:09:36.630
or like just get people into it.

00:09:36.630 --> 00:09:37.573
- Yeah.

00:09:37.573 --> 00:09:40.080
I heard that you, do you
get injured before filming?

00:09:40.080 --> 00:09:41.331
Is this a thing you do?

00:09:41.331 --> 00:09:42.630
- I got sciatica, I pinched my nerve.

00:09:42.630 --> 00:09:44.063
- I got that pregnant once.

00:09:44.063 --> 00:09:45.810
- Oh my God.
- I thought I was gonna die.

00:09:45.810 --> 00:09:46.650
- Was it down one side?

00:09:46.650 --> 00:09:48.331
- Down the whole left side.

00:09:48.331 --> 00:09:49.843
- I had the same thing.

00:09:49.843 --> 00:09:51.090
- I wanted to hurt someone.

00:09:51.090 --> 00:09:52.290
Because I wanted them to feel

00:09:52.290 --> 00:09:53.940
just for a second what I was feeling.

00:09:53.940 --> 00:09:55.337
- Yeah, its unbearable.

00:09:55.337 --> 00:09:58.140
And if you haven't experienced
sciatica, it is debilitating.

00:09:58.140 --> 00:10:00.840
It's just, it's all you can think about.

00:10:00.840 --> 00:10:02.640
- And then people talk to you
and you just wanna hurt them.

00:10:02.640 --> 00:10:03.960
And I'm like, "I don't
know why I wanna hurt you,

00:10:03.960 --> 00:10:05.370
but I just, I'm in pain.

00:10:05.370 --> 00:10:06.203
Don't talk to me".

00:10:06.203 --> 00:10:07.320
- I wanted to chop my leg off.

00:10:07.320 --> 00:10:08.454
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:10:08.454 --> 00:10:09.960
- "If that fixes it, I'll do it".

00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:11.761
It was just all I could think off.

00:10:11.761 --> 00:10:13.140
- But I hear that this
happens when you film things.

00:10:13.140 --> 00:10:14.220
You get injured it.

00:10:14.220 --> 00:10:15.053
- Yeah.

00:10:15.053 --> 00:10:16.410
It's like the stress manifests.

00:10:16.410 --> 00:10:18.432
- Is your superstitious thing you do.

00:10:18.432 --> 00:10:19.920
I need to injure myself.

00:10:19.920 --> 00:10:20.760
It will do well.

00:10:20.760 --> 00:10:22.350
- I need to feel pain when I'm creative.

00:10:22.350 --> 00:10:23.790
- [Kelly] Very method.

00:10:23.790 --> 00:10:25.470
- I always get something wrong with me.

00:10:25.470 --> 00:10:27.240
And then it goes away as soon as I finish.

00:10:27.240 --> 00:10:28.110
- Oh my gosh.

00:10:28.110 --> 00:10:30.781
There is a lot to unpack there in therapy.

00:10:30.781 --> 00:10:31.961
- It's all emotional.

00:10:31.961 --> 00:10:33.930
- So it's emotional.

00:10:33.930 --> 00:10:34.763
Okay.

00:10:34.763 --> 00:10:36.090
So I heard that maybe
you're doing Star Wars.

00:10:36.090 --> 00:10:36.990
Are you gonna do a Star Wars film?

00:10:36.990 --> 00:10:39.153
- Yeah, I've been developing
that for a few years.

00:10:39.153 --> 00:10:41.861
- Okay.

00:10:41.861 --> 00:10:43.860
- Any film, but that one in particular,

00:10:43.860 --> 00:10:45.270
it's something I'd
really like to get right.

00:10:45.270 --> 00:10:46.620
So I don't wanna rush it.

00:10:46.620 --> 00:10:47.453
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:10:47.453 --> 00:10:49.410
- Just gonna bubble along on the side.

00:10:49.410 --> 00:10:50.790
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- It's exciting.

00:10:50.790 --> 00:10:52.410
- Our family we were Star
Wars fans growing up.

00:10:52.410 --> 00:10:53.460
So yeah.
- [Taika] Me too.

00:10:53.460 --> 00:10:54.634
- Very cool.

00:10:54.634 --> 00:10:55.467
- I wanna capture that joy

00:10:55.467 --> 00:10:58.530
and the entertainment of those
early ones that, you know.

00:10:58.530 --> 00:10:59.430
Like Empire Strikes Back

00:10:59.430 --> 00:11:01.631
and Return to The Jedi,
and all those ones.

00:11:01.631 --> 00:11:02.584
- [Kelly] The OG's.

00:11:02.584 --> 00:11:03.570
- I'm trying to figure that out.

00:11:03.570 --> 00:11:04.403
- [Kelly] Alright, take your time.

00:11:04.403 --> 00:11:05.721
- It'll happen.

00:11:05.721 --> 00:11:06.784
- 'Cause you'll do it
right when you do it.

00:11:06.784 --> 00:11:07.617
So take your time.

00:11:07.617 --> 00:11:09.450
Let's do another break while
you're taking your time.

00:11:09.450 --> 00:11:12.630
Taika's movie Next Goal
Wins is in theaters now,

00:11:12.630 --> 00:11:13.880
y'all gotta check it out.

